        "original_id": "adb1f047-dd6f-52f2-b6b0-53bccde07bee",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Naomi Watts, Scott Coffey\n- Works: Ellie Parker, For Love Alone, Hey Dad..!, Built Like Alaska's untitled third album\n- Organizations: Built Like Alaska\n- Places: Los Angeles, Oakdale, Modesto, Wave Parade\n- Topics: film production, acting careers, film scoring, music touring, album recording\n\nFacts:\n- Naomi Watts was born on 28 September 1968 and is an English actress and film producer.\n- Naomi Watts made her screen debut in the Australian drama film For Love Alone in 1986.\n- Naomi Watts then appeared in the Australian television series Hey Dad..! after her 1986 screen debut.\n- Ellie Parker is a 2005 American drama-comedy film written and directed by Scott Coffey.\n- Naomi Watts played the title character in Ellie Parker, a young woman struggling as an actress in Los Angeles.\n- In 2005, Built Like Alaska provided the score for Scott Coffey's film Ellie Parker.\n- In 2005, Built Like Alaska also spent much of the summer touring the United States.\n- Built Like Alaska later completed work on an untitled third album that the band recorded in Oakdale and Lucky Lew mixed at Wave Parade in Modesto.",
